From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ndamathia <47696354+OliverSolomon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:07:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Windows-style inline tools, rulers that follow the view,
 web font previews, Version History hooks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The mini toolbar shows straight after a double- or triple-click (the
  second click's drag never ended), carries Grow/Shrink Font, Bullets,
  Numbering and New Comment as on Windows, and sits above the context
  menu.
- Rulers measure the page in view once the caret's page scrolls away;
  double-clicking a ruler opens Page Setup.
- Font-box rows for web fonts that aren't loaded ask the host for their
  regular face (font_previews) and redraw once it arrives.
- host_versions: the title and File > Info open Version History through
  host_events; the title reads 'Name • Saved'; mode items show two lines.
- Text without em dashes in the strings these patches touch.
